      "start": 35.703625,
      "end": 57.4945,
      "lesson_progress": 0.3333333333333333,
      "text": "Multiplication and division describe the same equal-group relationship. If groups times group size gives the total, dividing the total by one known factor finds the other. An estimate provides a separate size check. Three equal groups of four make twelve. Sharing twelve into three equal groups gives four in each.",
